@tradition long-breakfast
// Long breakfast (weekly, seat 15). On Saturdays the galley keeps breakfast going until 10:00, with pancakes, for the
// crew who are off. The gathering is 08:00-09:30 (after the usual window), ending before the fortnightly harvest
// morning starts at 09:30, so the two never overlap on Deck 3. A meal tradition:
// meal: breakfast    (the sim engineer's field, still to be added to the grammar: going counts as your breakfast)
// Design note: plans/trad-notes-weekly.md.
k: 439
title: Long breakfast
when: weekly saturday
at: 08:00-09:30
min: 25
jitter: 20
where: 3 room Mess hall: mess-seat
hold: none
who: late-sleeper 85%, lingers-at-meals 80%, juniors 50%, everyone 40%
anim: talk
from: brennan
ties: galley meal=breakfast dish=pancakes until=10:00

== mail
- Long breakfast tomorrow: Saturday pancakes in the mess hall until ten. Sleep in. We'll keep the griddle warm.

== ask
- Long breakfast this morning. Pancakes until ten.
- I slept in on purpose. It's Saturday. There are pancakes.   #funny
- Coming down for pancakes? There's no rush. That's the whole point.   #warm

== here
- Pass the syrup? No, the other syrup.   #funny
- Third pancake. I'm not counting. You're not counting.   #funny
- No shift, no hurry. This is the life.   #warm

== thanks
- You take a stack of pancakes to a table in the sun lamps' light. Nobody's in a hurry.   #warm

== chatter
- Saturday pancakes are what gets me through the week.   #funny
- The long breakfast table is the only place you see the whole galley sitting down.
- Best thing about a day off: pancakes until ten.
